Description: Keel robot baseboard library (Python binding)
 libkeel drives the Keel robot baseboard on a Raspberry Pi 4: two motors
 behind a hardware enable gate, the safety MCU's heartbeat and arming
 handshake, six RGB LEDs, four buttons with indicator LEDs and the
 ultrasonic ranging connector. A built-in simulator runs the same safety
 state machine against the production MCU policy.
 .
 This package contains the Python module keel, which loads the system's
 libkeel.so.1 through ctypes and offers the whole API, a control-loop
 helper and typed exceptions, and the module keel.camera, which drives
 the Raspberry Pi camera through libkeel-camera.so.1 (libkeel-camera1,
 needed only for camera use; python3-numpy gives frames as arrays). The
 examples are in /usr/share/doc/python3-keel/examples.
